ize: medium; color: #000000;"><i>wildtype</i></span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #f8f8f8; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #6e5d00;">+</span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #f8f8f8; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #126c64;">+</span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #f8f8f8; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #9c334e;">+</span></td><td align="right" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">75</span></td></tr><tr><th colspan="4" align="right" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #cccccc; padding: 10px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">TOTAL =</span></th><td align="right" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">2,000</span></td></tr></table><p>The resulting phenotypes are summarized in the table above.</p> <h6>Question</h6> <p>Based on the traits expressed in the offspring, identify the <span style="color: DarkRed;"><strong>parental genotype combinations</strong></span>. These are the allele combinations that the parent fruit flies originally carried.</p> <p>More than one genotype will be correct. Select all that apply.</p>
PROMPT_2ACE_1DD9
loadMacros('parserCheckboxList.pl');
$choice_1 = <<'LITERAL_2ACE_1DD9_CHOICE_1';
hty
LITERAL_2ACE_1DD9_CHOICE_1
$choice_2 = <<'LITERAL_2ACE_1DD9_CHOICE_2';
ht+
LITERAL_2ACE_1DD9_CHOICE_2
$choice_3 = <<'LITERAL_2ACE_1DD9_CHOICE_3';
h+y
LITERAL_2ACE_1DD9_CHOICE_3
$choice_4 = <<'LITERAL_2ACE_1DD9_CHOICE_4';
h++
LITERAL_2ACE_1DD9_CHOICE_4
$choice_5 = <<'LITERAL_2ACE_1DD9_CHOICE_5';
+ty
LITERAL_2ACE_1DD9_CHOICE_5
$choice_6 = <<'LITERAL_2ACE_1DD9_CHOICE_6';
+t+
LITERAL_2ACE_1DD9_CHOICE_6
